      <tbody>
        {roles.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="k">{row.role}</th>
            <td data-col="provider and model" class="k">{row.agent}</td>
            <td data-col="access">{row.access}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </Table>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>enforced by</dt><dd><a href={repoFile("scripts/review-feature.sh")}><code>review-feature.sh</code></a> (provider independence), <a href={repoFile("scripts/lib/review-data.sh")}><code>scripts/lib/review-data.sh</code></a> (findings across rounds)</dd>
      <dt>docs</dt><dd><a href={href("docs/detailed-workflow/#review-the-implementation")}>Review the implementation</a>, <a href={href("docs/detailed-workflow/#decide-what-to-do-with-review-findings")}>Decide what to do with review findings</a></dd>
      <dt>built in</dt><dd><a href={pull(12)}>PR #12</a> and <a href={pull(14)}>#14</a> (triage), <a href={pull(164)}>#164</a> (your decisions), <a href={pull(222)}>#222</a> (earlier rounds)</dd>
    </dl>
  </Section>

  <Section id="risk" title="Risk-proportionate workflow">
    <Fragment slot="note">Configured in <a href={repoFile(".agents/policies/risk.conf")}><code>risk.conf</code></a>. <a href={href("docs/risk-policy/")}>Risk policy</a> in the docs.</Fragment>
    <p class="lede">A typo and a change to the merge gate do not deserve the same process. Every feature gets a risk level, low, medium or high, computed from what it changes; the level picks the model of each writing role and what the review rounds require.</p>
    <figure class="plain">
      <svg class="lines" viewBox="0 0 1100 160" role="img" aria-labelledby="risk-t" aria-describedby="risk-words">
        <title id="risk-t">How the level is set: the classes of the changed paths, the escalations and your hint each give a level; the highest counts and nothing lowers it. The review can raise it again: an impact on the architecture classified as major or breaking makes the feature high.</title>
        <path class="branch" d="M1000 80 L960 40 H800 L760 80"/>
        <text class="note" x="880" y="28" text-anchor="middle">major or breaking impact: high</text>
        <path class="l2" d="M80 80 H1000"/>
        <circle class="dot" cx="80" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="80" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Changed paths</text><text class="sub k" x="80" y="137" text-anchor="middle">risk.conf</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="300" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="300" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Escalations</text><text class="sub" x="300" y="137" text-anchor="middle">tests, check lists, policies</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="530" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="530" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Your hint</text><text class="sub k" x="530" y="137" text-anchor="middle">risk: high | --risk</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="760" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="760" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Level</text><text class="sub" x="760" y="137" text-anchor="middle">the highest; never lowered</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="1000" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="1000" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Review</text><text class="sub" x="1000" y="137" text-anchor="middle">impact on the architecture</text>
      </svg>
      <ol class="words" id="risk-words">
        <li><b>Changed paths</b><small class="k">.agents/policies/risk.conf</small><p class="cond">The highest class of any changed path; a path no class names gets the default.</p></li>
        <li><b>Escalations</b><small>tests, check lists, fixtures, manifests, policies, prompts, schemas</small><p class="cond">A changed existing one makes the feature high.</p></li>
        <li><b>Your hint</b><small class="k">risk: high | risk: medium | --risk</small><p class="cond">Before the first session.</p></li>
        <li><b>Level</b><small>the highest counts; nothing lowers it</small><p class="cond">It picks the model of each writing role and what the review rounds require.</p></li>
        <li><b>Review</b><small>classifies the impact on the architecture</small><p class="cond">Major or breaking makes the feature high.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
    <pre role="region" class="excerpt" aria-label="Excerpt of the description of pull request 249"><span class="src">{bare(pull(249))} · excerpt</span>Risk: medium
- documentation/src/pages/about.astro: no class of .agents/policies/risk.conf names it; the default is medium
[...]
- profile: none

Triage mode: full (the default; .agents/policies/risk.conf of the base has no 'medium: triage:' line)</pre>
    <Table>
      <caption>The sources of the level; the highest one counts. From <code>scripts/lib/risk.sh</code> and the header of <code>risk.conf</code>, read from the base branch, so a feature cannot relax the rules it is classified by.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">source</th><th scope="col">what raises the level</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Paths</th><td data-col="what raises the level">The highest class of any changed path; a path no class names gets the default. As shipped: default medium, the workflow's own gate files high, no low class.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Escalations</th><td data-col="what raises the level">Always high: a changed or removed line of an existing test or of the check lists, any change to a shared test fixture, a changed existing manifest, and a changed existing file under <code>.agents/policies/</code>, <code>.agents/prompts/</code> or <code>.agents/schemas/</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">The reviewer</th><td data-col="what raises the level">An impact on the architecture classified as major or breaking.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">You</th><td data-col="what raises the level">The Issue label <code>risk: high</code> or <code>risk: medium</code>, or <code>--risk</code>, before the first session.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </Table>
    <p>Any source can raise the level; nothing lowers it. A low level exists only under <code>profile: light</code>, which adds a low class for documentation and process files and lets a low feature go without a review, said in the commit and the pull request, with your approval of the merge. Under both profiles every commit needs the full verification and only you merge. High always keeps every control.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>key</dt><dd><code>profile: light | standard</code>; per level, <code>&lt;level&gt;: verification | review | triage: &lt;value&gt;</code></dd>
      <dt>model per level</dt><dd><code>implementer@high: claude fable</code> in <a href={repoFile(".agents/agents.conf")}><code>agents.conf</code></a></dd>
      <dt>try it</dt><dd><code>./scripts/check-risk.sh</code> in a feature worktree prints the level and its reasons</dd>
      <dt>built in</dt><dd><a href={pull(194)}>PR #194</a> (the level), <a href={pull(202)}>#202</a> and <a href={pull(211)}>#211</a> (models per level), <a href={pull(214)}>#214</a> (profiles), <a href={pull(229)}>#229</a> (your hint)</dd>
    </dl>
  </Section>

  <Section id="unattended" title="Safe unattended execution">
    <Fragment slot="note">Limits in <a href={repoFile("scripts/run-feature.sh")}><code>run-feature.sh</code></a>, profiles in <a href={repoFile("scripts/lib/agent.sh")}><code>scripts/lib/agent.sh</code></a>. <a href={href("docs/detailed-workflow/#run-a-feature-unattended")}>Run a feature unattended</a> in the docs.</Fragment>
    <p class="lede">An unattended run has nobody to ask and nobody watching. <code>run-feature.sh</code> takes a feature from its Issue to an open pull request without questions, inside fixed limits, and leaves a record of every step.</p>
    <figure class="plain">
      <svg class="lines" viewBox="0 0 1100 160" role="img" aria-labelledby="unattended-t" aria-describedby="unattended-words">
        <title id="unattended-t">An unattended run: run-feature.sh starts the implementer under the unattended profile, verifies, and runs the review rounds, with the fixes of each round, until an open pull request; there the run ends, and you merge. An agent that needs your decision stops the run with status 3.</title>
        <path class="branch" d="M680 80 L640 40 H320 L280 80"/>
        <text class="note" x="480" y="28" text-anchor="middle">FIX_NOW: the fixes, then the next round</text>
        <path class="l2" d="M80 80 H1040"/>
        <circle class="dot" cx="80" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="80" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Start</text><text class="sub k" x="80" y="137" text-anchor="middle">run-feature.sh</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="280" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="280" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Implement</text><text class="sub" x="280" y="137" text-anchor="middle">at most 4 sessions</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="480" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="480" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Verify</text><text class="sub" x="480" y="137" text-anchor="middle">at most 3 repairs</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="680" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="680" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Review</text><text class="sub" x="680" y="137" text-anchor="middle">at most 5 rounds</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="880" cy="80" r="10"/><text class="st" x="880" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Pull request</text><text class="sub" x="880" y="137" text-anchor="middle">the run ends</text>
        <rect class="gate" x="1030" y="70" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 1040 80)"/><text class="st" x="1040" y="117" text-anchor="middle">Merge</text><text class="sub" x="1040" y="137" text-anchor="middle">by you</text>
      </svg>
      <ol class="words" id="unattended-words">
        <li><b>Start</b><small class="k">run-feature.sh</small></li>
        <li><b>Implement</b><small>unattended profile; by default at most 4 sessions</small><p class="cond">BLOCKED: the run exits with status 3; the same command continues after your answer.</p></li>
        <li><b>Verify</b><small>by default at most 3 repairs of a failing verification</small></li>
        <li><b>Review</b><small>read-only; at most 5 rounds</small><p class="cond">FIX_NOW: the fixes, then the next round.</p></li>
        <li><b>Pull request</b><small>open; the run ends here and never removes a worktree</small></li>
        <li class="you"><b>Merge</b><small>by you</small></li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
    <ul class="rules">
      <li><b>Bounded permissions.</b> A writing agent runs under the <code>unattended</code> profile: anything that would ask is denied, and it gets no MCP servers or apps from your configuration. Reviewers and triage run <code>read-only</code>.</li>
      <li><b>Bounded effort.</b> At most 5 review rounds in a run, and by default 4 implementer sessions, 3 retries of a failing agent call and 3 repairs of a failing verification.</li>
      <li><b>Stops instead of guesses.</b> An agent that needs your decision ends with a <code>BLOCKED:</code> line and the run exits with status 3. Running the same command again continues where the feature stands.</li>
      <li><b>Never merges.</b> The run ends at an open pull request and never removes a worktree.</li>
    </ul>
    <pre role="region" class="excerpt" aria-label="Excerpt of the run record of feature 241"><span class="src">.agents/records/feature-241.jsonl · run of PR #249, excerpt</span>{record}</pre>
    <p>Every run leaves such a record on your machine: each step and its duration, the agent, model and level, the verification seconds, the findings and why a run stopped. <code>report-runs.sh</code> summarises it per feature and <code>analyze-runs.sh</code> lets a read-only analyst propose changes; <a href={href("#learn")}>the analysis of 28 October 2026</a> is how Codeyard found what to change in itself.</p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>records</dt><dd><code>.agents/records/feature-&lt;issue&gt;.jsonl</code> in the primary checkout, ignored by Git, format <code>run-record/v1</code> (<a href={`${repoFile("docs/development.md")}#run-records`}><code>docs/development.md</code></a>)</dd>
      <dt>docs</dt><dd><a href={href("docs/technical-reference/#what-is-recorded-on-your-machine")}>What is recorded on your machine</a></dd>
      <dt>built in</dt><dd><a href={pull(136)}>PR #136</a> to <a href={pull(140)}>#140</a> (records), <a href={pull(223)}>#223</a> (stops)</dd>
    </dl>
  </Section>

  <Section id="authority" title="Human authority">
    <Fragment slot="note">Configured in <a href={repoFile(".agents/policies/guardrails.conf")}><code>guardrails.conf</code></a>. <a href={href("docs/configuration-and-security/#changes-that-need-the-owner")}>Changes that need the owner</a> in the docs.</Fragment>
    <p class="lede">No script merges. The decisions that matter stay with you: the requirements, the plan, the answers to questions, and the merge, and some pull requests only you may approve.</p>
    <figure class="plain">
      <svg class="lines" viewBox="0 0 1100 170" role="img" aria-labelledby="authority-t" aria-describedby="authority-words">
        <title id="authority-t">Your decisions: you agree the requirements and approve the plan; a feature asks you only when it needs a decision; a pull request that changes a protected path, has a major or breaking impact or no review needs your approval of exactly its commit; and only you merge.</title>
        <path class="branch" d="M780 90 L820 50 H970 L1010 90"/>
        <rect class="gate" x="885" y="40" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 895 50)"/>
        <text class="note" x="895" y="24" text-anchor="middle">protected path, major impact or no review</text>
        <path class="l1" d="M80 90 H300"/>
        <path class="l2" d="M300 90 H1010"/>
        <rect class="gate" x="70" y="80" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 80 90)"/><text class="st" x="80" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Requirements</text><text class="sub" x="80" y="147" text-anchor="middle">you agree them</text>
        <rect class="gate" x="290" y="80" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 300 90)"/><text class="st" x="300" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Plan</text><text class="sub k" x="300" y="147" text-anchor="middle">finish-planning.sh</text>
        <rect class="gate-o" x="530" y="80" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 540 90)"/><text class="st" x="540" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Questions</text><text class="sub" x="540" y="147" text-anchor="middle">you answer, when asked</text>
        <circle class="dot" cx="780" cy="90" r="10"/><text class="st" x="780" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Pull request</text><text class="sub" x="780" y="147" text-anchor="middle">rules from the base branch</text>
        <rect class="gate" x="1000" y="80" width="20" height="20" transform="rotate(45 1010 90)"/><text class="st" x="1010" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Merge</text><text class="sub" x="1010" y="147" text-anchor="middle">only you</text>
      </svg>
      <ol class="words" id="authority-words">
        <li class="you"><b>Requirements</b><small>you agree them with the Project Grill</small></li>
        <li class="you"><b>Plan</b><small class="k">finish-planning.sh</small></li>
        <li class="ask"><b>Questions</b><small>you answer, only when a feature asks</small></li>
        <li><b>Pull request</b><small>the rules are read from the base branch</small><p class="cond">A protected path, a major or breaking impact, or no review: your approval of exactly this commit.</p></li>
        <li class="you"><b>Merge</b><small>only you; no script merges</small></li>
      </ol>
    </figure>
    <p>Your approval is needed when a feature changes a protected path, when the reviewer classifies its impact on the architecture as major or breaking, or when there is no review. Always protected: every ADR, the CI workflows, the files that carry out the gate, and a changed or removed line of the check lists. The rules are read from the base branch, so a feature cannot loosen its own gate.</p>
    <pre role="region" class="excerpt" aria-label="Excerpt of the description of pull request 222"><span class="src">{bare(pull(222))} · excerpt</span>Merge approval:
- required from the project owner, for exactly this commit
[...]
- scripts/review-feature.sh: the file defines or carries out the workflow and its gate
- the independent review classified the impact on the architecture as major: [...]</pre>
    <div class="split">
      <div><h3>Codeyard enforces</h3><ul>
        <li>The risk level, and that no agent lowers it</li>
        <li>A reviewer of another provider, read-only</li>
        <li>Verification before review and before commit</li>
        <li>The completion gate and the triage rules</li>
        <li>Rules read from the base branch</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div><h3>Your GitHub settings enforce</h3><ul>
        <li>A ruleset on <code>main</code> that requires a pull request and the CI check; <code>doctor.sh</code> warns when it is missing</li>
        <li>Code-owner review, once you replace the placeholder in <a href={repoFile(".github/CODEOWNERS")}><code>CODEOWNERS</code></a></li>
        <li>An approval the agent cannot give itself: needs a separate agent identity, <a href={issue(99)}>not built yet</a></li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>checks</dt><dd><a href={repoFile("scripts/check-guardrails.sh")}><code>check-guardrails.sh</code></a> locally, and the Guardrails job of <a href={repoFile(".github/workflows/guardrails.yml")}><code>guardrails.yml</code></a> on every pull request</dd>
      <dt>settings</dt><dd><a href={href("docs/github-setup/")}>GitHub setup</a> in the docs</dd>
      <dt>built in</dt><dd><a href={pull(100)}>PR #100</a> (the gate), <a href={pull(200)}>#200</a> (approval requests and the content tree)</dd>
    </dl>
  </Section>
